          "description": "Successful jq exit 0: {status: \"success\", tool: \"jq\", target: string, exit_code: 0, result: any JSON value|null, stdout: string|null, stderr: string|null}. If stdout is exactly one non-null JSON document, result contains that value and stdout=null. If the single JSON document is null, json.loads succeeds but the helper cannot distinguish it from its parsed=None sentinel, so result=null and the original stdout (normally `null\\n`) is retained. Empty, multi-value, or otherwise non-single-document stdout also yields result=null with raw stdout retained. Nonzero jq result uses the same keys with status=\"tool_error\" and propagates jq's exit code. Non-existing file, missing executable, or 120-second timeout: {status: \"error\", tool: \"jq\", message: string}, exiting 2/3/4. Missing file argument prints usage to stderr and exits 1 without JSON.",
